# HTML blank-line formatting

When creating or editing HTML files, keep **at most one consecutive blank line** between blocks of code.

## Rule

- **Allowed:** one empty line between sections, tags, or logical blocks
- **Not allowed:** two or more consecutive blank lines with no code on them

Collapse runs of blank lines down to a single blank line.

## Example

```html
<!-- BAD: 4 consecutive blank lines between sections -->
    </section>



    <section class="next">

<!-- GOOD: 1 blank line -->
    </section>

    <section class="next">
```

Four empty lines → one empty line (three removed). Same for two or three consecutive blank lines: always reduce to one.

## Scope

Apply when writing or refactoring HTML under `src/` (pages, partials in `_page-components`, icons, etc.). Do not add trailing blank lines at EOF beyond a single final newline if the file already ends that way.
